// per-insert — the MAPVS/MAPKS credits free them at reclaim) but read bit 1
// (kconsume: free the discarded fresh key on an overwrite, #4881/#4885).
// Bit 2 = `owncols` (#4353 grow-leak, general case #5335): the map's key AND
// value columns BOTH read back as snapshots (i32 columns snapshot-copy, string
// columns snapshot with per-element retain), so no keys()/values() read aliases
// the raw column buffers — the map is the SOLE owner of its keys[]/vals[]
// buffers and the register map_set's grow path may free the superseded buffer
// (__fern_arr_push_owned) instead of leaking it. i64/f64/struct/generic
// columns keep owncols=0 (their reads still raw-alias — irlower's
// map_kv_elem_flag 1). wasm ignores bit 2 (its map already frees old buffers
// on grow).
