// (i32/string pointer), 1 = i64/u64, 2 = f64. The x86-64 and arm64 runtimes store
// the value 8-byte unconditionally (movq / str x), so they ignore it. On wasm the
// i32-celled $__fern_map_set can't hold an 8-byte value directly: widekind 1
// (i64/u64) routes to $__fern_map_set_w64 (an 8-byte cell boxed into the i32
// column); widekind 2 (f64) stays deferred to the AST backend via
// wasm_ir_deferrals_ok. #5253.
